# Private ~/.config/pizdato-evening.env, chmod 600; never commit credentials.
# Default model access reuses OPENROUTER_API_KEY from ~/.config/pizdato-channel.env.
PIZDATO_EVENING_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash
# Optional stronger reviewer model (proofreader, editor, verifier; morning too):
# PIZDATO_EDITOR_MODEL=openai/gpt-6.1-sol
# Optional OpenAI-compatible endpoint instead of OpenRouter, e.g. Nous Portal. It serves EVERY role and
# both slots, so PIZDATO_EVENING_MODEL (and PIZDATO_MORNING_MODEL if set) must be models it serves:
# PIZDATO_LLM_BASE_URL=https://inference-api.nousresearch.com/v1
# NOUS_API_KEY=
# PIZDATO_EVENING_MODEL=openai/gpt-6.1-sol
# PIZDATO_EDITOR_MODEL=openai/gpt-6.1-sol
# Keys are bound to hosts: OPENROUTER_API_KEY only for openrouter.ai, NOUS_API_KEY only for nousresearch.com,
# PIZDATO_LLM_API_KEY for any host. PIZDATO_LLM_DIALECT=openrouter|openai overrides detection.
# Rollback: remove PIZDATO_LLM_BASE_URL and set PIZDATO_EVENING_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash again.
# Reasoning effort for OpenAI reasoning models (low|medium|high; default low). Reviewers = proofreader,
# editor and verifier. Measured on Nous Portal with full history: one review takes 5–14 s (low), 11–36 s (high).
# PIZDATO_REASONING_EFFORT=high
# PIZDATO_EDITOR_REASONING_EFFORT=high
# Run `bash ~/.local/share/pizdato-evening/tick.sh --check` after any change: it proves plain replies,
# strict JSON from every configured model and tool calls from the evening model, without publishing.
# Existing Composio For You consumer credential for the existing account:
COMPOSIO_CONSUMER_KEY=
